sfying to blame something that doesn't harm everyone. I get that. And honestly, that's part of why the debate around fast food is so heated — because people see healthy fast food eaters and feel the argument is exaggerated. But from a scientific perspective, a risk factor doesn't need to be universal to be real and important. I'm not trying to convince you that fast food is the biggest villain. I just want you to see why public health experts, based on the data, consider it a significant piece of the puzzle — even if it doesn't fit every individual story perfectly.
